# Compiled artifacts of the C assembler. Regenerate with: cd mac-c && make
# EVERYTHING generated now lands in mac-c/build/ - objects and both
# executables (mac-as, test_mac). `make clean` removes the whole directory.
mac-c/build/

# NOTE: Build/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It holds the assembler's output
# (ASYMB/BSYMB symbol dumps, LIST1-5 listings) and is kept in the repository
# so the result is browsable without running a build. It is still fully
# regenerable: cd mac-c && ./scripts/build/build_tss_assysa.sh

# The build scripts stage the TSS source into Build/ (and Build/drum/) as the
# assembler's INPUT, but those copies are byte-identical to src/ — the single
# clean source. No point tracking duplicates; they are recreated every build.
Build/TSS[1-5].SYMB
Build/drum/TSS[1-5].SYMB

# Disposable nd100x disc images (multi-MB). There is exactly ONE working disc
# set: Build/bringup/, created on demand by `make prepare`. Everything else here
# is a throwaway test copy and must never be committed.
Build/bringup/
Build/coldstart_test/
Build/scratchtest/
Build/autobringup/
Build/realmac/
Build/cmdtest/

# Transient build logs / captured assembler stdout+stderr under Build/ —
# regenerated by build_tss_*.sh (run() writes err_/write_; drum/minit write
# build.err/out). Never commit these; only the real artifacts belong in git.
Build/*/build.err
Build/*/build.out
Build/err_*.txt
Build/write_*.txt

# Python bytecode caches (bringup/, tools/).
__pycache__/
